    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and both its tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule with minimal structural impact:\n\n**Behavior:** `POST /api/owners` now accepts an optional `registrationDate`. When supplied it's kept; when omitted it defaults to the server's current date. `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes (each a small, self-contained addition):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, the generated request DTO, response DTO, and both MapStruct mappings all pick up the field automatically \u2014 no hand-written DTO/mapper edits.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with a plain getter/setter. `LocalDate` serializes to ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` by default.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 added a two-line default inside the existing build step (a tiny, single-method class, so almost no surrounding complexity): if the mapped owner has no registration date, set it to `LocalDate.now()`. This keeps the defaulting out of the large `Owner` and `OwnerMapper` classes.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column (hsqldb runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be explicit; the h2/mysql/postgres schemas already rely on `ddl-auto=update` and omit even `email`, so leaving them is consistent) and added the corresponding `NULL` to the ten positional seed inserts.\n\nI placed the default logic in `BuildOwner` rather than a `@PrePersist` hook or the mapper specifically because those would have landed the cost inside the high-complexity `Owner`/`OwnerMapper` classes \u2014 the biggest structural-impact lever the task warned about.",
